LICENCE AND TERMS FOR data/
===========================

The MIT licence in the repository root only covers the SOFTWARE in this repository. It does NOT 
cover the datasets in this directory. Each item in data/ retains the terms of its source and this 
file is the authoritative statement. Section 1 lists every file and points at the section that 
governs it.

    1.  File Provenance
    2.  DALME-Marseille corpus and annotations .... CC BY 4.0
    3.  CLTK Latin lemmata ........................ MIT
    4.  Lewis, An Elementary Latin Dictionary ..... CC BY-SA 3.0
    5.  Dictionnaire de l'Occitan Médiéval ........ non-commercial
    6.  Stanza benchmark table .................... ODC-By 1.0
    
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. File Provenance
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   PATH                                        WHAT IT IS                              SEE
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   marseille_test_corpus.csv                   database export, 47,345 rows            (2)
   corpora/la_marseille-ud-base.conllu         corpus converted to CoNLL-U             (2)
   corpora/la_marseille-ud-base-fixed.conllu   after the three mechanical corrections  (2)
   corpora/la_marseille-ud-full.conllu         the whole corpus parsed                 (2)
   gold/                                       200-sentence gold standard, 2 stages    (2)
   seeds/base/                                 sampled sentences, placeholder syntax   (2)
   seeds/predictions/                          after pre-annotation by the prior model (2)
   seeds/corrected/                            after hand correction, the training set (2)
   marseille_lemmata.json                      domain lexicon, gold-free (5,254)       (2)
   marseille_lemmata_with_gold.json            the same before 61 entries were removed (2)
   lemmata/marseille_lemmata.txt               lemma inventory of the corpus           (2)
   reference/inventory_metadata.csv            per-record date, place, document type   (2)
   reference/brat_annotation_times.csv         minutes spent correcting each batch     (2)
   reference/dalme_occitan_lemmata.txt         Occitan lemmata contributed by DALME    (2)
   evaluation/                                 model predictions and scores            (2)
   evaluation/results_with_gold_lexicon.json   scores under the uncorrected lexicon    (2)
   baseline_results.json                       construction-specific baselines         (2)
   lemmata/cltk_lemmata.txt                    CLTK lemma list, extracted              (3)
   lemmata/lewis_lemmata.txt                   Lewis headwords, extracted              (4)
   reference/dom_online_lemmata.txt            15,992 Occitan headwords, DOM           (5)
   reference/stanza-ud-2.5-performance.csv     published Stanza benchmark scores       (6)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. DALME-Marseille corpus and annotations       Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The DALME-Marseille transcriptions, the document metadata, and the part-of-speech, lemma,
   morphological, and dependency annotation layered over them are released together under the
   Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence.
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   This governs every file marked (2) in section 1.

   ATTRIBUTION, to accompany any copy or derivative:

       DALME-Marseille corpus. Documentary Archaeology of Late Medieval Europe (DALME),
       https://dalme.org. Licensed under CC BY 4.0. Morphological and syntactic annotation by
       Gabriel H. Pizzorno.

