4. Lewis, An Elementary Latin Dictionary (1890)                                 CC BY-SA 3.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Charlton T. Lewis, An Elementary Latin Dictionary. American Book Company, New York,
   Cincinnati and Chicago, 1890. The text is public domain and the CLTK digitisation is 
   released under Creative Commons ShareAlike 3.0.
   https://github.com/cltk/cltk_lat_lewis_elementary_lexicon

   Shipped as the extract lemmata/lewis_lemmata.txt. The raw source is not redistributed here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Dictionnaire de l'Occitan Médiéval            non-commercial | notice must travel with it
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   reference/dom_online_lemmata.txt is 15,992 headwords collected from the online Dictionnaire
   de l'Occitan Médiéval (DOM), founded by Wolf-Dieter Stempel and published by the Bayerische
   Akademie der Wissenschaften. Responsible for content: Prof. Dr. Maria Selig and
   Dr. Monika Tausend.

       Lemma list: https://dom-en-ligne.de/lemlist.php
       Legal notice: https://dom.badw.de/fr/mentions-legales.html

   DOM grants a bespoke permission, which the legal notice states as follows:

       "Die Urheberrechte dieser Web-Site liegen vollständig bei der Bayerischen Akademie der
        Wissenschaften."

       "Diese Seiten und Dokumente dürfen nicht kommerziell verwertet werden."

   Copying, printing, and distributing the pages and documents is permitted for informational
   purposes, non-commercially, PROVIDED EVERY COPY CARRIES THE COPYRIGHT NOTICE:

       © Bayerische Akademie der Wissenschaften — Dictionnaire de l'Occitan Médiéval (DOM),
       https://dom.badw.de. Not for commercial use.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. Stanza benchmark table                           ODC-By 1.0, as far as Stanford states it
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   reference/stanza-ud-2.5-performance.csv holds the published test-set scores of the 100 
   Stanza models released for Universal Dependencies 2.5, as distributed by the Stanza project. 
   It is used only to place this corpus's scores in context, in one figure.

   Stanza's performance page carries the only licence statement the project appears to make about
   this material:

       "To the extent that The Trustees of Leland Stanford Junior University have ownership and
        rights over these language packs, all these Stanza language packs are made available
        under the Open Data Commons Attribution License v1.0."
       https://stanfordnlp.github.io/stanza/performance.html

   Attribution: Stanza, Stanford NLP Group. https://stanfordnlp.github.io/stanza/
